  "visualBrief": "Native connected monastery ensemble with integral west dormitory/museum facade, eleven normal bays each side of a central three-bay pavilion, recessed lower arcade glazing, tall upper windows and pitched terracotta roofs. Four slender crocketed dormitory turrets in front/rear end pairs and a separate broad stone-domed church campanile. True open two-storey chamfered cloister, triple lower shafts/paired upper lights, medallion parapets and conical pinnacles; lawn, paths and low circular fountain. Church Latin-cross mass, giant pointed south windows, projecting tiered sculptural south portal, pierced roof rail, distinct rear/chancel roofs, attached northern monastic rooms and separate large western court.",
